{"name":"Sweet Tart","hex":"#eaaea9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"tart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sharp to the taste; acid; sour.","High or too high in acidity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of small open pie, or piece of pastry, now typically containing jelly (US) / jam (UK) or conserve, or sometimes other fillings (chocolate, custard, egg, butter, historically even meat or other savory fillings).","A melt (block of wax for use in a tart burner)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tart"}],"entries":[{"title":"SweeTarts","blocks":[{"text":"SweeTarts are sweet and sour candies invented under the direction of Menlo F. Smith, CEO of Sunline Inc., in 1962. The candy was created using the same basic recipe as the already popular Pixy Stix and Lik-M-Aid products, all of which are currently manufactured by Ferrara Candy Company, a division of Ferrero."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Nestle-SweeTarts-Candies.jpg/330px-Nestle-SweeTarts-Candies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SweeTarts"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"},{"title":"Tart","blocks":[{"text":"A tart is a baked dish consisting of a filling over a pastry base with an open top not covered with pastry. The pastry is usually shortcrust pastry; the filling may be sweet or savoury, though modern tarts are usually fruit-based, sometimes with custard. Tartlet refers to a miniature tart; an example would be egg tarts. The categories of \"tart\", \"flan\", and \"pie\" overlap, with no sharp distinctions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Raspberry_tart.jpg/330px-Raspberry_tart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tart"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Giant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg/500px-Giant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Giant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg/1280px-Giant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Giant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg/500px-Giant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Giant Chewy SweeTarts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiant-Chewy-SweeTarts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg/500px-Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Boys_Pilfering_Molasses_by_George_Henry_Hall.jpg/1280px-Boys_Pilferi